import AxQM.Core.FourGateReachableWireTower
import AxQM.Postulates.API.FourGateReachableRotation
import AxQM.Postulates.API.FourGateReachableWireMonoid

/-!
# The whole reachable single-qubit rotation submonoid on a register wire, as tower gates
(N&C Exercise 4.43, whole-submonoid stage)

The universality argument of Exercise 4.43 exhibits the *abstract* reachable gate set of
`Concrete.exists_phase_smul_mem_closure_reachableCircuits` as circuits of the
`H, S, CNOT, Toffoli` gates. Its rotation half uses the single-qubit reachable rotations placed
on a wire — the matrices `Concrete.singleQubitOnWire enc j g` for **every** `g` in the submonoid
`Concrete.reachableRotations θ`, not only its four generators. The register lift in
`AxQM/Core/FourGateReachableWireTower.lean` handles the four *generators*
`R_z(±θ), R_x(±θ)` on a wire (`quditPowTower_congr_rotZWireEvolution` /
`quditPowTower_congr_rotXWireEvolution`); this file closes the submonoid, transferring the lift from
the generators to *every* product of them.

The single-wire-placement monoid-homomorphism facts this lift turns on —
`Evolution.qtowerSingleWire_id` / `Evolution.qtowerSingleWire_comp` (`qtowerSingleWire n i` sends
the identity gate to the identity and a composition `g · h` to
`(qtowerSingleWire n i g) · (qtowerSingleWire n i h)`) — are in
`AxQM/Core/QtowerSingleWireGate.lean`.

## What is formalised

The register-level reachable-rotation wire submonoid `reachableRotationWireEvolutions n t θ` — the
submonoid of `Evolution (qudit (2ⁿ⁺¹))` generated by the four wire gates
`rotZWireEvolution (n+1) t (±θ)`, `rotXWireEvolution (n+1) t (±θ)`, the register-gate counterpart of
`Concrete.reachableRotations θ` placed on wire `t` — is defined in
`AxQM/Postulates/API/FourGateReachableWireMonoid.lean`, together with the matrix→submonoid bridge
`quditGate_singleQubitOnWire_mem_reachableRotationWireEvolutions`.

* `exists_reachableRotationGate_congr_quditPowTower_eq` — **the whole-submonoid lift**: every member
  of `reachableRotationWireEvolutions n t θ`, transported onto the control tower via the register
  bridge `quditPowTower n`, is the gate `qtowerSingleWire n t.rev E` for some
  `E ∈ reachableRotationGates θ` — a reachable single-qubit rotation gate (built, with measurement,
  from `H, S, CNOT, Toffoli`) placed on the single tower wire `t.rev`. Proved by
  `Submonoid.closure_induction`: on the four generators it is the register lift together with the
  membership of the corresponding `rotZGate (±θ)` / `rotXGate (±θ)` in `reachableRotationGates θ`;
  on `1` and on products it is the two monoid-homomorphism facts on each side —
  `Evolution.congr` (`Evolution.congr_id` / `Evolution.congr_comp`) and `qtowerSingleWire`
  (`Evolution.qtowerSingleWire_id` / `Evolution.qtowerSingleWire_comp`) transporting the closure of
  `reachableRotationGates θ` under `mul_mem` / `one_mem`.

So the *whole* single-qubit reachable-rotation submonoid on a register wire — the exact shape
`⋃ j, singleQubitOnWire enc j '' reachableRotations θ` in which the reachable rotations enter the
abstract `reachableGateSet` — is realised, on the tower, by the reachable rotation gates.
`AxQM/Postulates/API/FourGateReachableWireMonoid.lean` identifies the register wire matrix gate
`quditGate (singleQubitOnWire finFunctionFinEquiv t g)` with a member of
`reachableRotationWireEvolutions n t θ`, which this lift then applies to.
-/

open scoped InnerProductSpace TensorProduct

noncomputable section

namespace AxQM

/-! ### The register reachable-rotation wire submonoid and its lift -/

/-- **The whole reachable-rotation wire submonoid lifts to tower gates.** Every member `F`
of the register submonoid `reachableRotationWireEvolutions n t θ`, transported onto the control
tower via the register bridge `quditPowTower n`, is the gate `qtowerSingleWire n t.rev E`
applying a reachable single-qubit rotation gate `E ∈ reachableRotationGates θ` to the tower wire
`t.rev`:

  `Evolution.congr (quditPowTower n) F = Evolution.qtowerSingleWire n t.rev E`.

Extends the generator-level register lift (`quditPowTower_congr_rotZWireEvolution` /
`quditPowTower_congr_rotXWireEvolution`) from the four generators to the whole submonoid: by
`Submonoid.closure_induction`, the generators give the register lift with the corresponding
`rotZGate (±θ)` / `rotXGate (±θ)` a generator of `reachableRotationGates θ`, and the `1` / product
cases are the monoid-homomorphism laws of `Evolution.congr` (`Evolution.congr_id` /
`Evolution.congr_comp`) and `qtowerSingleWire` (`Evolution.qtowerSingleWire_id` /
`Evolution.qtowerSingleWire_comp`), landing in `reachableRotationGates θ` by `one_mem` / `mul_mem`.
Since a reachable rotation gate is a `{H, S}`-composition around the measurement-realised `R_z(θ)`
(the Exercise 4.41 circuit `rzThreeFifthsCircuit`), every reachable single-qubit rotation on a
register wire is thereby a genuine circuit on a tower wire. -/
theorem exists_reachableRotationGate_congr_quditPowTower_eq {n : ℕ} {t : Fin (n + 1)} {θ : ℝ}
    {F : Evolution (qudit (2 ^ (n + 1)))} (hF : F ∈ reachableRotationWireEvolutions n t θ) :
    ∃ E ∈ reachableRotationGates θ,
      Evolution.congr (quditPowTower n) F = Evolution.qtowerSingleWire n t.rev E := by
  induction hF using Submonoid.closure_induction with
  | mem x hx =>
    rcases hx with rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl
    · exact ⟨rotZGate θ, Submonoid.subset_closure (by simp),
        quditPowTower_congr_rotZWireEvolution n t θ⟩
    · exact ⟨rotZGate (-θ), Submonoid.subset_closure (by simp),
        quditPowTower_congr_rotZWireEvolution n t (-θ)⟩
    · exact ⟨rotXGate θ, Submonoid.subset_closure (by simp),
        quditPowTower_congr_rotXWireEvolution n t θ⟩
    · exact ⟨rotXGate (-θ), Submonoid.subset_closure (by simp),
        quditPowTower_congr_rotXWireEvolution n t (-θ)⟩
  | one =>
    exact ⟨1, one_mem _, by
      simp only [Evolution.one_def, Evolution.congr_id, Evolution.qtowerSingleWire_id]⟩
  | mul x y _ _ ihx ihy =>
    obtain ⟨Ex, hEx, hxeq⟩ := ihx
    obtain ⟨Ey, hEy, hyeq⟩ := ihy
    refine ⟨Ex * Ey, mul_mem hEx hEy, ?_⟩
    rw [Evolution.mul_def x y, Evolution.congr_comp, hxeq, hyeq, Evolution.mul_def Ex Ey,
      Evolution.qtowerSingleWire_comp]

end AxQM

end
